{
 "_about": "Query sets for the Domain feed collector (scripts/feed-collect.mjs). Edit this file to tune what is collected; no code change needed. Tier 1 runs first (competitors, new entrants, Millrose filings, financing at the largest builders). Tier 2 widens to all 100 builders. The baseline set is the naive alert we compare against and is never mixed into the targeted set. News search uses Bing News RSS, which only handles short plain queries, so each query is a name plus one or two terms; `must` lists words that have to appear in the headline or snippet for a result to be kept (Bing pads thin results with unrelated headlines). `gdelt` queries are boolean and full-text; they are best-effort because the free GDELT API rate-limits hard. Google News RSS is not used: its robots.txt disallows automated access to the search feed.",
 "window_days": 90,
 "user_agent": "domain-intel-research/1.0 (research use)",
 "rate_ms": {
  "www.bing.com": 1400,
  "api.gdeltproject.org": 6500,
  "data.sec.gov": 600,
  "efts.sec.gov": 600,
  "default": 1000
 },
